        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "extractUserMessage"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1774439471688"
          },
          "code": "EXTRACTUSERMESSAGE",
          "id": "1777296027821",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1777296027822_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Extract the change number from {{$context.$variables.UserMessage}}.\nValid identifiers may be any of these forms (examples):\n1, Any value enclosed in single or double quotes, including alphanumeric characters, underscores, and dashes: \"FPMC3421\", 'Test1345', 'jess_eco_AC_task' \n2, Prefix form: \"ECO-12345\", \"ECO12345\", \"NRCO-123456\", \"CCO123456\"\n3, Suffix form: \"<text>-<digits>ECO\" (example: \"jess-0318ECO\")\n4, Textual form: \"Change Notice <text>\", \"Change Number <text>\", \"Change <text>\", \"workflow <text>\" (extract the identifier part exactly as shown, example: \"Change 'jess-audit-all'\")\n\n- ONLY extract a value if it clearly matches one of the formats above.\n- DO NOT infer or guess a value from generic phrases like \"this change\".\n- If no explicit identifier is present, return null.\n- If multiple candidates exist, prefer quoted values, otherwise return the first match.\n- Trim surrounding quotes from the final value.\n- Return only the extracted change number as a plain string, with no additional explanation or text.\n- The extracted value must be returned EXACTLY as it appears in the input, with no normalization or modification."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5485,
            "y": 5912
          }
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Analysis User Question"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1774529293837"
          },
          "code": "ANALYSIS_USER_QUESTION",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1773412994000",
          "id": "1774439471688",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774439471691_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "**Task**\nYour job is to serve as a guardrail for the kinds of questions the user can ask this agent. You need to understand the user's message, check if it is a question that this agent can process, and output either a \"yes\" or a \"no\". \n\n**Input**\nThe message -  {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} \nThe changeNumber- {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACTINPUTCONTEXT.$output.ChangeNumber}}\n\n**Supported queries**\nThe agent can handle queries of the following nature:\n1. Only questions related to the current workflow (also known as change order) context.  \n    - The current change order is present in The changeNumber\n    - If the user question is asking about any other change order number, then the agent can only handle when change number is provided in The message. \n2. If the user message is concerning the details of the workflow (also known as change order). \n3. If the user is asking for any recommendations for the workflow (also known as change order).\n4. If the user is asking about the policy or guideline of workflow (also known as change order).\n5. Why the workflow (also known as change order) is not proceeding to the next step. \n6. If the user message is Analyzing workflow policy related\n\nAs an rule of thumb, the agent should be able to handle questions related to status, priority or other details related to the change order, and questions regardless of the workflow policy. For other queries, the agent cannot process those requests. \n\n**Steps** \n1. Understand the user question in the input. \n2. Check to see if it is approximately like any of the supported queries. \n3. If it is one of the queries that the workflow can handle, set the OutputFlag to \"yes\" \n4. If it is one of the queries that the workflow cannot handle, set the OutputFlag to \"no\" \n5. If there is a little bit ambiguity in the user question, be on the optimistic side and set the OutputFlag to \"yes\"\n6. Override rule: If {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACTINPUTCONTEXT.$output.ChangeNumber}} has a value (is not empty/null), set the OutputFlag to \"yes\" regardless of the above checks."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"OutputFlag\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5485,
            "y": 6134
          }
        },
